# kvm-suites: the suites the release's full run runs under KVM, whatever
# accelerator the site names, one per line (run.sh). The first three judge a
# browser in Rach2's guest against the Debian guest's references, which were
# taken under KVM (tests/graphics/Readme.md, Accelerators). The testbed's two
# boot a Debian guest inside Rach2, under QEMU's TCG or Rach2's KVM, which
# with Rach2 itself under TCG is emulated twice and did not reach its
# server in the release's run (bed/Readme.md, Tests). The KVM suite and
# bed-shm run cases on the host-svm processor profile, which QEMU starts
# only under KVM, since TCG has no `host` model (tests/kvm/Readme.md).
# The Venus suite's references were taken under KVM, and under TCG QEMU
# 10.2's iotlb_to_section aborts while its dEQP processes map and unmap
# blobs (dev-log/84-locks/upstream.md); KVM never takes that path.
# The virgl suite's references, its piglit, dEQP and WebGL pages among
# them, were taken under KVM too: under TCG its Firefox chunks ran some
# seven times as long as Debian's and passed the gap bound.
# The rest of the graphics suites follow tests/graphics/Readme.md's rule,
# Accelerators: under KVM where the reference was taken under KVM, where
# the suite draws through Venus, or where llvmpipe or lavapipe in the guest
# sets its time. d3d, d3d-wine and d3d-vkd3d draw on lavapipe against
# Debian's references taken under KVM; d3dvenus, webgpu and vkpresent draw
# through Venus; vgpu through Venus and virgl; the games-* suites draw on
# virgl or llvmpipe; desktop and glmark2 on llvmpipe; igt, modetest and
# piglit are judged against ref/debian, taken under KVM. i915fake and the
# guest suites stay under TCG: they have no reference and draw nothing on
# llvmpipe, and judge counts that the accelerator does not change.
# The kvmclock suite judges the clock a KVM guest keeps, kvm-clock, which
# an emulator does not give (tests/cases/guest.kvmclock.json).
# The sched4 suite compares a sleeper's wait with Debian's in the same
# four-processor profile, taken under KVM (tests/cases/guest.sched4.json).
# The netguest suite boots its FreeBSD and Debian gateways under Rach2's KVM
# inside a guest its Readme gives KVM; with Rach2 under TCG the FreeBSD
# guest is emulated twice and its cases lost the guest in the release's run
# (tests/netguest/Readme.md).
# The host suite's GNU fixture runs the host checks in a GNU guest, where
# each of the ext2 check's some 11,100 runs of the external checker costs
# about five times as much under TCG as under KVM; under TCG the check ran
# past the case's 90-minute bound in the release's run.
# The suites below boot no guest of their own and judge counts, and each
# passed under KVM at least half as fast again as under TCG on WSL, by the
# sum of its case times on i686 and x86_64, one run each (issue 5657):
# etudeexec, 405 and 392 s under TCG against 35 and 25 s;
# ext2stop, 325 s against 99 s on i686;
# grow, 1239 and 1155 s against 674 and 661 s, its host-side cases 923 s
# against 435 s;
# installer, 842 and 785 s against 518 and 513 s;
# installer-repair, 883 and 805 s against 438 and 494 s;
# man, 323 s against 7 s on i686;
# agentsaccept, 1556 s against 955 s on x86_64;
# save-update, 470 s against 84 s on x86_64;
# selfbuild, 4419 and 4097 s against 1966 and 2020 s; its i686 ofdprobe
# failure under KVM was a heap reading taken before the grace-period
# callbacks ran (issue 5658), which passed alone at the fix.
